s accessible by any user on their  mobile device or on their desktop okay  so we've got the foundation of this app  created and it's already ready  for the team to be using so they can  capture their inspections digitally  instead of just with pen and paper  so they're already using the app they're  already collecting these tickets in the  application  the real gains from this particular app  are going to come by  incorporating this ai model specifically  using some of that existing data  to build an ocr model so tony can you  walk us through  that stage right now  so peter just talked about how to build  this cool quality control  app that allows you to move from a  paper-based process to a digital process  where instead of employees filling out  paper forms  they're using this mobile app to take  pictures of these tickets and to  transcribe the information in them so  what i'm going to talk about next  is how to take advantage of the data  that is now being collected via this  mobile app  so you can think of every time your  employee uses this app  they take a photo of one of these  quality control tickets  and then enters in information so we're  building up a data set  now we can use ai and machine learning  to take advantage of the data that we've  collected  and further enrich the app by making it  more efficient and easier to use  so let me give you a quick tour of some  of the ai features  that are available in app sheet so i'm  going to navigate to the intelligence  tab in the app sheet editor  and the first feature i want to show you  is the smart assistant feature  so the smart assistant feature enables a  google assistant like experience  inside of your mobile app but customized  to your business domain  so once you flip this switch in the  editor you get your own  custom assistant that understands  natural language  let me give you a couple examples so to  access the assistant  i go to this view that's available in  the side menu of my app  called assis