is on to  go from the picture of an inspection  ticket to these extracted fields  next i need to specify the image column  in this case there's just a single  column in my data set called image  this is going to be the inputs of the  model then i choose the output  these are the columns in the data set  that i want to predict in this case it's  automatically selected  the other columns in the table like  condition part number  quantity and so on so this is the  how i specify the model and when i press  save what's going to happen  is actually it's going to look at the  data that's already in my table  these examples you see over here on the  right and it's going to use a machine  learning model  to figure out common patterns of where  these  values appear in the images so i'm going  to press save  cool now that the page has reloaded the  ocr model has been trained and we can  actually inspect it to see what it  learned from the data set  so i'm going to scroll down a little bit  and  you can see here below uh my model  i have the examples from my training set  if i click on them you can see that  it's found out where in the image the  columns  in my table are found so for example  this yellow piece right here at the  bottom  is identified as where the description  is located in the image  and it identified that the word rejected  up here corresponds to the condition  field in the  the same table so it's gone through  these ten or so examples that we've  already collected via  regular use of the app and figured out  how to generalize from it  and uh now we can use it to identify uh  where these fields are automatically in  new images so let me give you an example  of that  so i'm going to go back to the app here  and i'm going to click on the new  inspection  button at the bottom so you can see this  is the form that the app creators have  been using to fill out the app so far  so now i'm going to upload a new image  to the form  this is an image that wasn't already 