 on the words that  appear in the description  you could then use that categorization  to route failures or rejections to the  right team  so this is another way that you can use  cloud a high-powered machine learning  without having to be a programmer  great yeah so and the example that we  just showed and then and then also the  extension that you just described  um is there a particular example of a  customer that has built  a similar solution and you is using it  with their team that you can  describe a little bit yeah so as an  example we've got a customer from the  construction industry who's starting to  roll out an ocr powered app  and so what they have is an app sheet  powered  workflow already where they have truck  drivers uh driving  picking up goods and delivering them to  work sites  and every time they do this they have to  use their mobile phone to take a picture  of like a trucking ticket or a receipt  um they're already using an app sheet  app to do this and then a qa person  downstream uh goes through those images  that they  uh the truck drivers captured and  manually transcribes all the information  from them like the shipment weights and  the date and the time  um but because they already have this  workflow uh built on an app sheet app  they're able to just extend it further  uh using the the platform's ocr  capabilities so now the qa person  doesn't have to go through and  transcribe every ticket  which would take you know minutes for  every ticket and they have hundreds of  these tickets  uh now they can uh just actually have  the ocr system automatically fill out  the forms and then they can just verify  to make sure it's  correct so this just saves tons of time  for these qa people  yeah very cool thanks tony so finally um  can you just give us  a quick synopsis or description of what  is around the corner for ai  in the option platform yeah so there's a  couple things i can highlight  so one is the platform itself  is becoming more and more intelligent  giving  app creators suggestions as they build  their app  making it easier to go from an idea to a  fully functioning app  a second way that it's uh we're  improving things is  allowing you to build workflows based on  uh cloud ai  [Music]  technology so for example having a  workflow where you upload a document  it's automatically categorized routed to  the right person  um and classified further and the third  direction  is deeper integrations with google  cloud's machine learning offerings  to make it even easier for apps to  understand your unstructured data  that's great thanks for sharing tony  it's real exciting to see  sort of how the platform the apps  themselves are continuing to get  new ai features so just to recap what  tony's described  and and what we've shown here in in  these couple demos is having ai built  into the no code apps as well as into  the authoring environment  it really just boils down to apps being  easier to  to make and and being capable of really  powerful functionality  and really importantly all along the way  because  this is uh entirely in a no code  environment it's really easy to control  with  organizational level policies that are  real simple to set up  and they're easy to maintain long term  so with that thank you tony for your  work making this functionality available  and for helping demonstrate it today  and thank you everyone who has joined  the session  and are watching this video i know i  speak for the team when i say that we're  excited to have new users joining and  creating really interesting and powerful  solutions for their own teams there's a  real strong community of app creators  here  at app sheet and throughout google and  and honestly all over the world  that are ready to help share ideas and  help you get started  in the platform so if you'd like to  learn more and try it out  you can find app sheet in google cloud  or directly at appsheet.com  thanks
 

